### A walk through every requirement, in order, for the IntelliJ HTTP Client (or VS Code REST Client).
### Run the steps top to bottom on an empty database (docker compose down -v, then ./gradlew bootRun):
### each step's title says what to expect.
###
### The service trusts X-Forwarded-For from localhost, so the header stands in for the client IP.
### 212.77.98.9 is in Poland (wp.pl), 46.4.0.1 in Germany (Hetzner), according to the DB-IP database.

### 1. Create a coupon with 2 uses for Poland: 201, Location, code stored as WIOSNA, currentUses 0, createdAt set
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "wiosna", "maxUses": 2, "country": "PL"}

### 2. The same code in another letter case: 409 COUPON_CODE_ALREADY_EXISTS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "Wiosna", "maxUses": 10, "country": "DE"}

### 3. Read it back in any case: 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/wIoSnA

### 4. user-1 from Poland uses it: 201, Location points to the redemption
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### 5. user-1 again: 409 COUPON_ALREADY_REDEEMED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### 6. user-2 from Germany: 403 COUPON_COUNTRY_NOT_ALLOWED (no use is consumed)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 46.4.0.1

{"userId": "user-2"}

### 7. No X-Forwarded-For: the client is localhost, whose country is unknown, so 403 COUPON_COUNTRY_NOT_ALLOWED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "user-2"}

### 8. user-3 from Poland takes the last use: 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-3"}

### 9. user-4 after the limit: 409 COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-4"}

### 10. user-3 retries after the limit: 409 COUPON_ALREADY_REDEEMED, the reason that actually applies
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-3"}

### 11. The counter: 200 with currentUses 2
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA

### 12. Unknown coupon: 404 COUPON_NOT_FOUND
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/NIE-MA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### 13. Did user-1's use go through? 200 with redeemedAt
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions/user-1

### 14. A user who never used it: 404 REDEMPTION_NOT_FOUND
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/WIOSNA/redemptions/user-9

### 15. Invalid input: 400 VALIDATION_FAILED listing every bad field (code, maxUses, country)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "", "maxUses": 0}

### 16. Not JSON: 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{not json

### 17. A coupon valid only through December 2099 (validUntil is exclusive): 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "zima", "maxUses": 100, "country": "PL", "validFrom": "2099-12-01T00:00:00Z", "validUntil": "2100-01-01T00:00:00Z"}

### 18. Using it now, before its period starts: 409 COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/coupons/ZIMA/redemptions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 212.77.98.9

{"userId": "user-1"}

### 19. Outcomes so far, by type: search for coupons_redemptions_total
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/prometheus

### 20. Readiness: UP while the database is reachable
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health/readiness
